          color = g[r][c]\n            if (r, c) in seen:\n                continue\n            stack = [(r, c)]\n            seen.add((r, c))\n            cells = []\n            while stack:\n                rr, cc = stack.pop()\n                cells.append((rr, cc))\n                for dr, dc in ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)):\n                    nr, nc = rr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if (0 <= nr < h and 0 <= nc < w and\n                            (nr, nc) not in seen and g[nr][nc] == color):\n                        seen.add((nr, nc))\n                        stack.append((nr, nc))\n            r0 = min(x for x, y in cells)\n            c0 = min(y for x, y in cells)\n            shape = frozenset((x - r0, y - c0) for x, y in cells)\n            comps.append((color, cells, shape))\n\n    # Identify the L-shaped guide: its pixels occupy the top and left\n    # edges of its bounding box, with no other pixels.\n    guide = None\n    for color, cells, _ in comps:\n        r0 = min(r for r, c in cells)\n        r1 = max(r for r, c in cells)\n        c0 = min(c for r, c in cells)\n        c1 = max(c for r, c in cells)\n        shape = {(r - r0, c - c0) for r, c in cells}\n        expected = ({(0, c) for c in range(c1 - c0 + 1)} |\n                    {(r, 0) for r in range(r1 - r0 + 1)})\n        if len(shape) == len(expected) and shape == expected and len(cells) >= 10:\n            guide = (color, cells)\n            break\n\n    if guide is not None:\n        guide_color, guide_cells = guide\n        # Recolor the member of an identical-shape pair nearest the guide.\n        for i in range(len(comps)):\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(comps)):\n                if comps[i][2] != comps[j][2]:\n                    continue\n                def distance(component):\n                    return min(abs(r - rr) + abs(c - cc)\n                               for r, c in component[1]\n                               for rr, cc in guide_cells)\n                target = i if distance(comps[i]) < distance(comps[j]) else j\n                for r, c in comps[target][1]:\n                    g[r][c] = guide_color\n                return g\n\n    return g\n```\n{\"action\": \"submit\"}","steps":[],"action":{"type":"submit"}},{"step":70,"kind":"reprompt","phase":"act","t0":1792666444.107,"t1":1792666480.467,"alias":"task-edaf0752","message":"Your program was checked on demo pair 2 at no cost and its output is wrong. It gave\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 2 2 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 6 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4\n2 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 2 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2 2 6 6 6 6 6 6 2 2 4 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 0 0 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 0 0 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 2 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2\n4 4 4 4 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 0 0 0 0 2 4 4 2\n6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 6 0 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 6 0 0 0 0 2 2 4 4 4 2 2 2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 0 0 0 2 2 2 6 0 0 0 0 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2 2 4 2\n2 2 0 0 2 2 2 2 2 6 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 6 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 4 2 2\n2 0 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 6 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2\n0 0 0 0 0 0 2 2 2 6 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2\nwhere the pair's output is\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 6 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 2 2 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2\n0 0 0 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 6 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4\n2 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 2 2 2 2 6 6 2 2 2 2 2 4 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2 2 6 6 6 6 6 6 2 2 4 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 0 0 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 0 0 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 2 4 4 2 2 2\n2 2 2 2 2 2 2 0 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 2 4 2 2 2\n4 4 4 4 2 2 2 2 2 2 2